* text=auto eol=lf

# D-13 (#483): pin the self-hosted font binaries as binary. `text=auto` above
# would otherwise leave it to git's NUL-byte heuristic, and this repo also runs
# core.autocrlf=true — a woff2 that ever got line-ending-converted would be
# silently corrupted (the face fails to decode, and the app falls back with no
# build error). Explicit beats heuristic for a file whose corruption is invisible
# until render.
*.woff2 binary

# #737 C1 re-score follow-up: the same hazard, found the hard way. `text=auto`
# above plus this repo's `core.autocrlf=true` line-ending-converted six
# `.github/pr-evidence/*.png` blobs during a routine `git add -A` — twice in one
# session, invisible in a diff, fatal to the image. A screenshot is evidence;
# evidence that silently rots is worse than none. Explicit beats heuristic for
# any file whose corruption does not fail a build.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
